ecome a thing of the past long before this point; but this is still an above-average film, in large part because of the screenplay that stays so faithful to the original. The character designs are slightly more western-looking than one is accustomed to seeing in anime.\n\n(Source: pelleas.net)"},"tags":[{"name":"Fairy Tale","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Foreign","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Desert","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Magic","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Kids","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Middle East","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Male Protagonist","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Royal Affairs","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Class Struggle","rank":60,"spoiler":false}],"titles":{"display":"Aladdin and the Wonderful Lamp","english":"Aladdin and the Wonderful Lamp","native":"アラジンと魔法のランプ","romaji":"Sekai Meisaku Douwa: Aladdin to Mahou no Lamp","synonyms":[]},"trailer":null,"visibility":"general"}